From: Pranav Prashant Thombre <pthombre@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:33:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] Support buffered SSE with external token staging
 (#3382)

## What does this PR do?

Capture-prefixed requests with `stream: true` returned HTTP 422 when
external token staging was enabled. Allow Chat Completions, Responses,
and Anthropic Messages clients to use Gym's existing buffered SSE replay
with externally staged training tokens. The compaction Responses adapter
is covered by the same integration tests.

Keep worker requests non-streaming after request overrides and reject
conflicting static or per-request streaming overrides. Convert Responses
output before fingerprinting so reasoning and tool-call continuations
resolve the correct captured parent. Generation completes before SSE
replay, so this provides protocol compatibility without reducing time to
first content. Training reconstruction reads the staged tokens.

Add 27 route-level cases covering JSON/SSE requests, evaluation capture
on/off, worker request enforcement, response IDs, internal-field
stripping, token reconstruction, and two-call reasoning/tool
continuations.

## Validation

- 826 relevant Gym tests passed, including all 27 new integration cases,
the capture and streaming suites, and the vLLM and compaction adapter
suites.
- Real Qwen3-0.6B tool rollout through Gym HTTP, the NeMo-RL HTTP
worker, vLLM, and TransferQueue passed (Slurm job `3747841`): two
committed calls, answer `4`, reward `1.0`, and reconstruction of 234
tokens including 27 training tokens with finite logprobs.
- Full `pre-commit run --all-files` passed.
- Fern check passed with zero errors and one warning.

